   $q$What is the effect of keeping Teodora's chair empty through the warm-up and the first run of the overture?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It builds expectation from the rumors, so her small, apologetic entrance undercuts what readers were led to expect.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It proves the rumor that she walks out of commitments, since she does not come back at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It allows Felix to take over the principal chair for the entire rehearsal without her.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows that the conductor had forgotten to tell the orchestra that she was joining them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It builds expectation from the rumors, so her small, apologetic entrance undercuts what readers were led to expect.$q$, $q$The delay lets the rumors grow, and then she arrives shorter than pictured, with camp stickers, whispering an apology. She does arrive, so the delay does not confirm she walks out.$q$, 'draft', '4589bd8d-5c00-5678-a18c-486ae90cdcf4')
